        "original_id": "f6479047-6af0-5c50-8398-3a640ad4d2b5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Tropicana Products, PepsiCo, Pepsi-Cola Company, The Coca-Cola Company\n- People: Anthony T. Rossi\n- Products: Mountain Dew, Mello Yello\n- Places: Bradenton, Florida, United States, Canada\n- Topics: ownership, acquisitions, founding, competition\n\nFacts:\n- Anthony T. Rossi was an Italian immigrant who founded Tropicana Products in 1947 in Bradenton, Florida, in the United States.\n- In August 1964, the Pepsi-Cola Company acquired the Mountain Dew brand and production rights from Tip, and Mountain Dew distribution then expanded more widely across the United States and Canada.\n- On March 1, 1979, The Coca-Cola Company introduced Mello Yello as a highly caffeinated, citrus-flavored soft drink to compete with PepsiCo's Mountain Dew.\n- Since 1998, Tropicana Products has been owned by PepsiCo.\n- Tropicana Products grew from 50 employees to more than 8,000 employees by 2004, expanded into multiple product lines, and became one of the world's largest producers and marketers of citrus juice.\n- Anthony T. Rossi lived from September 13, 1900 to January 24, 1993.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
